    "# Efficient ResNet Challenge — One-click distillation (≤ 5M params)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Runs inside a Kaggle Notebook** (competition data is attached automatically, nothing to download).\n",
    "Before running: right sidebar → **Session options → Accelerator → GPU T4 x2** (or P100).\n",
    "\n",
    "Pipeline:\n",
    "1. Find the competition files under `/kaggle/input`\n",
    "2. Load the 50k training images + labels from the competition files, hold out a validation split\n",
    "3. Wide pre-activation ResNet-18 variant, **~4.8M params** (asserted below)\n",
    "4. Fast training: all data on GPU, GPU-side augmentation (crop + flip + cutout), mixed precision, OneCycle LR, label smoothing\n",
    "5. **CutMix** (mixes patches of two training images + their labels), **EMA** (running average of the weights, used for prediction), **SAM** optimizer (seeks flat minima that generalize better)\n",
    "6. **One-click knowledge distillation**: this notebook first trains `N_TEACHERS` teacher models from scratch (different seeds), then trains the student — same ≤5M architecture, from scratch — on the true labels *and* the teachers' averaged soft predictions. Only the student is used for the submission.\n",
    "7. Predict test set with multi-view TTA (flips + small shifts) → `submission.csv`\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to run:** Accelerator → GPU T4 x2, then **Save Version → Save & Run All (Commit)**. Takes ~4 hours with the defaults; you can close the tab."
   ]
